"The recurrence risk was assessed based on the patient's clinical profile, including an age of 70 and a PSA of 9.3, alongside the clinical T-stage of cT1c derived from the digital rectal examination. The Cox model predicts a recurrence time of 11.4 months, with no recurrence event observed during the follow-up period. This prediction reflects the baseline risk associated with these specific patient characteristics, though long-term outcomes remain subject to individual biological variability."